Zedu Backend Local Setup Guide - this guide explains how to clone, install, configure, and run the Zedu Telex backend locally, the backend is a Go application and uses dependencies such as PostgreSQL, Redis, RabbitMQ, MongoDB, Elasticsearch, MinIO, and Centrifugo to run its development.

STEP 1
What You Need
Before starting, you need:

Git
Go
Make
VS Code (recommended)
Internet connection
Enough disk space
PostgreSQL 
Redis 
MinIO 
MongoDB
RabbitMQ 
Elasticsearch 
Firebase (Service Account Key) 
Stripe account (for API key) 
Centrifugo 

Make sure all services are installed and running locally


STEP 2
Download Git

Go
Download: Go official downloads

Download Go 1.24.7 for Windows
Scroll down and Look for the Windows installer for 64-bit PCs:
go1.24.7.windows-amd64.msi
Download that .msi file.
If your computer uses a different architecture, scroll down and check for it and download the .msi file
Download and install: 
MakePostgreSQL
Redis 
MinIO 
MongoDB
RabbitMQ 
Elasticsearch 
Firebase (Service Account Key) 
Stripe account (for API key) 
Centrifugo 


STEP 3

The backend repository currently requires:
Go 1.24.0
Go toolchain 1.24.7

Verify Go:
go version
Expected:
go version go1.24.7 windows/amd64


STEP 4

Download Zedu  Backend to your local

run:
git clone  https://github.com/zeduchat/zedu-be

Enter Zedu-be Folder

run:
cd zedu-be


STEP 5
Request for staging credentials from Dev
Create a file in your zedu-be Folder  and name it app.env
Paste the Staging Credentials  into `app.env` Folder

STEP 6
Install Go dependencies. 

run: 
go mod tidy . 

STEP 7
Run the app. 

run:
go run main.go

STEP 8
Confirm that the API is running 

run:
`http://localhost:{port}`
